1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,392
Why does a spoon look broken in water?

2
00:00:02,692 --> 00:00:04,814
Pull it out, and it's perfectly straight.

3
00:00:05,314 --> 00:00:09,369
You see the spoon by the light that leaves it and reaches your eye.

4
00:00:09,669 --> 00:00:13,435
In water, light travels about a quarter slower than in air.

5
00:00:13,935 --> 00:00:18,793
So a ray leaving the water at a slant bends at the surface, tipping flatter.

6
00:00:19,093 --> 00:00:21,700
But your brain assumes the ray never bent.

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:27,332
It traces each ray straight back, to a spot higher than the spoon really is.

8
00:00:27,832 --> 00:00:30,541
The part in the air appears where it is.

9
00:00:30,541 --> 00:00:32,979
The part under water appears lifted.

10
00:00:33,279 --> 00:00:36,032
So the spoon seems to snap right at the surface.

11
00:00:36,532 --> 00:00:38,128
The spoon is not bent.

12
00:00:38,128 --> 00:00:39,071
The light is.
